The following words, terms and phrases, when used in this article and chapter, shall have the meanings ascribed to them in this section, except where the context clearly indicates a different meaning.
Animal means any living creature, both domestic and wild, except humans. The term "animal" also includes fowl, including chickens, turkeys, geese, ducks, pigeons, and similar fowl, as well as fish and reptiles.
Animal control officer means any individual designated by the county as an enforcement official for this article or chapter and shall include, but not be limited to, the county administrator or county manager, any county code enforcement officer and any officer within the Tattnall County Sheriff's Office. These officials shall have the authority to act on behalf of the county in investigating complaints, impounding, issuing citations and taking other lawful action as required to administer or enforce the provisions of this article and chapter. It shall be a violation of this article or chapter to interfere with enforcement official in the performance of their duties.
At large means off the property of an owner or possessor and not under the control of the owner or possessor, or a member of the owner's or possessor's immediate family, either by leash, cord, chain or other control or holding device.
Animal running at large means any animal causing a disturbance while not confined in an enclosure, or while not under the restraint or control of a leash, cord, chain or other control or holding device or while in the vicinity of the owner or possessor and not obedient to such owner's or possessor's commands; provided that, an animal is not running at large when it is confined within the limits of its owner's or possessor's property.
Enclosure means any covered, uncovered parcel of land (or portion of such parcel) where animals are kept.
Fence means any structure of wire, wood, stone or other material, which is of sufficient height and strength to act as a barrier against passage of the animal it is intended to enclose. A fence must be sufficient to prevent the animal from being able to jump, dig or escape confinement
Public nuisance means anything that harms or inconveniences the public or damages property, and public nuisance is also intended to mean and include, without limitation, any animal which:
(a) Is vicious;
(b) Causes or contributes to unsanitary conditions;
(c) Endangers, attacks, injures or kills another animal;
(d) Chases a vehicle or vehicles or creates an unsafe condition for the driver of any such vehicle;
(e) Is found repeatedly unrestrained;
(f) Excessively produces disturbing noises;
(g) Enters the property of a person or entity without the permission of such person or entity;
(h) Damages a person's or entity's property or creates an unsafe condition thereon;
(i) Annoys or endangers a person or persons; or
(j) Interferes with the enjoyment or use of property.
Owner means any natural person or legal entity including, but not limited to a corporation, partnership, firm or trust owning, possessing, harboring, keeping or having custody of an animal.
Possessor means any natural person or legal entity including, but not limited to a corporation, partnership, firm or trust possessing, harboring, keeping or having custody of an animal.
Under restraint means an animal that is securely enclosed or controlled within the boundaries of an owner's or possessor's real property or under the command or control of its owner or possessor.
(Ord. No. 2025-2, § I, 4-7-2025)

