240:
(a) When a dangerous dog is classified as such, an animal control officer shall notify the dog's owner of such classification.
(b) The notice to the owner will meet the following requirements:
(1) It will be in writing and mailed by certified mail to the owner's last known address;
(2) It will include a summary of the animal control officer's findings that formed the basis of the dog's classification as a dangerous dog;
(3) It will be dated and will state that the owner, within 15 days after the date shown on the notice, has a right to request a hearing on such officer's determination that the dog is a dangerous dog;
(4) It will state that the hearing, if requested, shall be before the county magistrate court;
(5) It will state that if a hearing is not requested, such officer's determination that the dog is a dangerous dog shall become effective for all purposes under this article on a date specified in the notice, which shall be after the last day on which the owner has a right to request a hearing; and
(6) It will include a form to request a hearing as provided in subsection (b) of this section, and it will schedule such hearing within 30 days after receiving the request.
(c) The magistrate court shall notify the dog owner in writing by certified mail of the date, time, and place of the hearing, and such notice will be mailed to the address of the dog owner shown on the request for hearing at least ten days prior to the date of the hearing. At the hearing the owner of the dog shall be given the opportunity to testify and present evidence and in addition thereto the court shall receive such other evidence and hear such other testimony as the court may find reasonable and necessary to make a determination either to sustain, modify, or overrule the animal control officer's determination that a dog is a dangerous dog.
(d) Within ten days after the date of the hearing, the court shall issue a final order, notifying the dog owner of its ruling on the matter, and the court shall mail such order via certified mail to the owner's address as shown on the request for hearing. If such order is that the dog is a dangerous dog, the order shall specify the date upon which the order is effective.
(Ord. No. 2025-2, § I, 4-7-2025)
